# Netlify redirects file — https://docs.netlify.com/routing/redirects/
#
# This is a static site with client-side routing (React Router): only
# index.html actually exists as a file, and pages like /shows or /bio
# are handled entirely in the browser by JavaScript after it loads. A
# static host doesn't know that by default — request /shows directly
# (or refresh the page while on it) and it looks for a literal file at
# that path, finds nothing, and 404s.
#
# This rule tells Netlify: for any path that doesn't match a real file
# (an image, a CSS file, etc), serve index.html instead (with a 200,
# not a redirect the browser would notice) and let React Router take it
# from there.
/*    /index.html   200
